    {
      "id": "1d06f8ef-51c7-4b8a-960a-e4f84c8ccea9",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -576,
        464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 1248,
        "height": 1136,
        "content": "## 1. Telegram & Album Buffer\n- **Telegram Trigger:** Captures incoming photos/albums.\n- **Filter & Parse Photo:** Extracts the highest-res photo, media group ID, and caption.\n- **Save to Data Table & Wait:** Temporarily stores split album items into an n8n Data Table and waits for 3 seconds to ensure all photos in the same album arrive safely before processing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7acfe613-688f-4f7c-9601-9b43b88db5d6",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        704,
        464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 1312,
        "height": 1136,
        "content": "## 2. AI Copywriting Pipeline\n- **Extract & Prepare:** Gathers album records and extracts the first non-empty caption.\n- **AI Content Generator (OpenRouter):** Acts as a professional copywriter. It analyzes the context and rewrites an engaging Facebook post with hooks, clean formatting, and hashtags.\n## 3. Media Processing & Facebook Upload\n- **Loop Over Items:** Iterates through each photo in the album array.\n- **Download & Upload:** Downloads binary files from Telegram servers and uploads them to Facebook as **unpublished media (`published = false`)** to retrieve their individual media FBIDs.\n- **Aggregate:** Combines all media FBIDs into an `attached_media` payload."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "75b089dd-4932-4ffa-b673-58281277be2a",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2048,
        464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1088,
        "height": 1136,
        "content": "## 4. Final Publishing & Feedback\n- **Merge Node:** Synchronizes the AI-generated text content and the aggregated media array.\n- **Publish Facebook Post:** Creates the final feed post combining text and photos, returning the post ID.\n- **Get Post URL & Notify:** Formats the Facebook post link and sends a success notification back to your Telegram chat with a clickable HTML link."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "87b75514-72be-4f74-84f4-1479fe8e455c",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1184,
        464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 576,
        "height": 1152,
        "content": "# \ud83d\ude80 Telegram Media Group to Facebook AI Automation\n## \ud83d\udccc Overview\nThis workflow solves the n8n limitation of handling Telegram albums (media groups), automatically refines captions using AI (OpenRouter), and publishes multi-photo posts directly to a Facebook Page.\n\n\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Prerequisites & Setup\nTelegram Bot: Connected to the Telegram Trigger node.\n\nn8n Data Table: Create a table named telegram_album with columns: media_group_id, file_id, caption, date.\n\nFacebook Graph API: Page Access Token with pages_manage_posts permission (Update your Facebook Page ID in the nodes).\n\nOpenRouter API: Configured for the AI Content Generator.\n\n\n## \u2699\ufe0f How It Works\nBuffer & Wait: Intercepts incoming Telegram photos, saves them to a Data Table, and waits 3 seconds to bundle full albums.\n\nAI Copywriting: The AI Agent polishes the caption with hooks and hashtags.\n\nStage & Publish: Downloads photos from Telegram, uploads them to Facebook as unpublished media, and publishes the final post.\n\nNotification: Sends a clickable HTML link of the live Facebook post back to your Telegram chat."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
